  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An engine operating between the boiling and freezing points of water will have</p><p>A. Efficiency more than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p><p>B. Efficiency less than the efficiency of a Carnot engine operating between the same two temperatures.</p><p>C. Efficiency equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p><p>D. Efficiency less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "B, C and D only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "A and B only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "B and D only",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "B and C only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The efficiency of Carnot engine can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>273</mn><mn>373</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>26</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>%</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the efficiency of the engine is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mi>engine</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>&#951;</mi><mi>carnot</mi></msub></math>.</p>"
  }
